// Title: Directory Service Restore Mode(DSRM) Registry Value Tampering
// Sigma ID: b61e87c0-50db-4b2e-8986-6a2be94b33b0
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nischal Khadgi
// Date: 2024-07-11 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, persistence, defense-impairment, T1556
// Description: Detects changes to "DsrmAdminLogonBehavior" registry value. During a Domain Controller (DC)
//   promotion, administrators create a Directory Services Restore Mode (DSRM) local administrator
//   account with a password that rarely changes. The DSRM account is an “Administrator” account that
//   logs in with the DSRM mode when the server is booting up to restore AD backups or recover the
//   server from a failure. Attackers could abuse DSRM account to maintain their persistence and
//   access to the organization's Active Directory. If the "DsrmAdminLogonBehavior" value is set to
//   "0", the administrator account can only be used if the DC starts in DSRM. If the
//   "DsrmAdminLogonBehavior" value is set to "1", the administrator account can only be used if the
//   local AD DS service is stopped. If the "DsrmAdminLogonBehavior" value is set to "2", the
//   administrator account can always be used.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://adsecurity.org/?p=1785
//   - https://www.sentinelone.com/blog/detecting-dsrm-account-misconfigurations/
//   - https://book.hacktricks.xyz/windows-hardening/active-directory-methodology/dsrm-credentials
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_dsrm_tampering.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\Control\\Lsa\\DsrmAdminLogonBehavior" and (not(RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000000)"))
